Z||000000||kevin||04-16-2000||08:16 PM||||It seems I developed a leak on the passenger side floor-board. It is definately green, suggesting a heater core problem. Can anybody provide aid as to what's involved in reaching the source of the leak. Please hurry, it smells bad!!||||reg||9
Z||000001||DXR_DAD||04-16-2000||08:35 PM||||R&R heater core that would be the best thong to do. Inside the black plastic box under the passanger side dash is were it is. If I remember there are two screws on top in the back that were hard to reach??? Remove the 2 heater hoses from the core, under the front hood the core comes out from the inside.<P>I think mine was 49.00 from the local parts house. Cheaper at wrenchead.com<P>But for the price, and to know it's new and you wont have any problems, Be like NIKE <BR>"JUST DO IT"||||reg||14
Z||000002||Patrick||04-16-2000||08:56 PM||||<BR>On my '87 it was easier to take the heater core out from the spare tire compartment side.||||reg||1
